course: dictionary
lesson: 14193
title: Perfectly still
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Motionless means not moving at all. It is completely still, like a statue or a photo. Look inside the word: motion means movement, and -less means without. So motionless means without any movement.
explain: «The cat sat motionless by the mousehole, waiting.» The word motionless tells you the cat did not move a whisker. Still and frozen are close in meaning, but motionless means no movement at all, not just a little.
explain: Stories use motionless to build tension. «The deer stood motionless in the trees, listening.» The reader feels the quiet and wonders what will happen next. Phrases you will meet often are lie motionless, stand motionless and remain motionless.
explain: Motionless can also be a safety word. «The climber lay motionless at the bottom of the rock.» If someone is motionless after a fall, they may be hurt, so tell an adult at once.
fact: Motionless means not moving at all; completely still.
fact: Motion means movement, and the ending -less means without, so motionless means without movement.
fact: In science, a ball lying on the grass is motionless until someone kicks it.
fact: In stories, a character who stays motionless may be hiding, frightened or hurt.
fact: A motionless person who has had a fall may need help, so tell an adult at once.
exercise: «The statue stood motionless in the square for a hundred years.» What does motionless mean? | Shiny and new | Moving very fast | Hard to lift | *Not moving at all
exercise: Ella's ball lay motionless on the grass until Sam kicked it. What is the ball doing before it is kicked? | Bouncing up and down | *Resting, with no movement at all | Rolling down the hill | Flying high in the air
exercise: «The guard had to ___ at the gate all night.» Which phrase fits best? | *stand motionless | run motionless | jump motionless | sing motionless
test: «The boy lay motionless in the long grass, hoping the wolf would pass.» Why might he be motionless? | Because he is dancing | Because he is very hungry for lunch | To win a race | *To hide and stay unseen
test: «The climber lay motionless at the bottom of the rock.» What might this suggest? | The climber is going very fast | The climber has just won a race | *The climber may be hurt and need help | The climber is doing a yoga pose
exam: Which sentence uses motionless correctly? | The motionless runner won the race by a mile | *The old tree stood motionless while the wind died down | The motionless dog barked at the post van | The motionless car sped down the busy road
